abstract: >-
  The Nayancode Workbench is a free, open-source collection of analysis studios that run entirely in the web
  browser: molecular docking with AutoDock Vina compiled to WebAssembly, sequence analysis and cloning, read mapping and variant calling with minimap2, samtools and bcftools compiled to WebAssembly,
  variant interpretation, bulk RNA-seq differential expression for any experimental design (validated against edgeR and limma) and enrichment, single-cell clustering,
  microbiome diversity, cheminformatics and QSAR, protein structure analysis and maximum-likelihood
  phylogenetics, and lab calculators (qPCR, dose-response, power) with publication-ready figures. Input files are analysed on the user's own computer, and every result records its own
  provenance and methods text.
